WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.350
Well, let's get crackin'.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.580
Let's-a-go.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.920
Stop messing around and start!

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.130
We saw a shooting star the other day...

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:38.050
...but Kagami said something about the
wishing three times thing being unrealistic.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.380
Shooting stars are so wonderful.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.840
I haven't seen many of them.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.350
It's difficult to see the stars from our house.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:46.560
Right...

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.560
Since your house is in the city, right?

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.520
I would probably be too amazed...

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.690
...to have time to make a wish.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:55.610
The sight of a dazzling, shining star...

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:58.030
...would fill you with feelings of joy.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:01.900
That could explain the myth
that shooting stars grant wishes.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:06.200
<i>Your honesty is what dazzles me.</i>

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.410
It's almost winter break.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.120
But we have finals first.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.460
Do you have any plans for winter break?

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:17.920
Nothing.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:18.550
Reminds me...

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.840
We haven't taken a vacation in a while.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.300
I went to Asakusa the other day.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.220
When was that?

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.640
You know how you get sleepy
on the train during winter?

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.310
<i>She missed her stop?!</i>

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:31.480
Huh?

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.520
But isn't that the opposite direction?

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.020
The train reached the end of
the line and turned around...

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.110
...and then I missed my stop again...

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.780
By the time I was conscious, we were in Asakusa.

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:41.820
Hey now.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.860
You can only miss your stop so many times.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.870
But it wasn't entirely a bad thing.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.540
Since I hadn't visited Asakusa in a while.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.210
Shouldn't be doing that right before finals.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:03:00.760
And I had a feeling I saw a girl in a
sailor uniform with a machine gun walk by...

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.670
What was that about?

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.260
Don't tell me someone was making a hit.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.300
And you know...

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.390
Sleeping more helps you grow more!

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:09.680
<i>You're growing?</i>

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:11.390
I got an even better one.

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:15.060
My dad pulled an all-nighter
and then went to turn in a manuscript.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.480
He got on an early-morning train but missed his stop...

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.480
...then it reached the end and made a U-turn...

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.360
...and when he woke up, he'd already missed his stop...

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.190
...and this happened a few more times.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:25.990
He started to wake up when
he got close to his station...

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:27.030
<i>Patrasche...</i>

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:27.200
...but he still ended up missing it.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.780
<i>I'm so tired...</i>

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:34.370
He was tired and wanted to get
home and sleep, but he couldn't get home.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.670
In the end, he no longer knew...

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:42.880
...which direction he was going whenever he woke up.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.090
Unbelievable...

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:48.090
I still wake up before my stop when I fall asleep.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:49.300
That's amazing!

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.720
How do you know?

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.060
Maybe she has an internal alarm clock.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:55.520
Though it doesn't work all the time.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:56.230
What was that?

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.350
Since she's always snacking away.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:03:59.690
Shut up!

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.400
But train seats are really warm...

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.240
...so you get really sleepy.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.650
That's true.

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:07.410
It's all warm and fuzzy...

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:10.660
...like you're sitting next to
the window in the classroom...

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:11.910
...on a sunny winter afternoon.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:12.790
What's this?

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:14.660
Covering for each other?

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.710
I-It's not like that!

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:17.670
The other day...

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:19.290
When I tried to wake you up on the ride home...

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:20.960
Hey, wake up!

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:21.880
We're there.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.510
Just five more minutes...

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:25.670
I mean it...

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.430
She yelled out half-asleep.

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:29.340
Everyone around us was laughing.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:33.600
One of my friends did that in class once.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:34.520
Sheesh.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.310
Birds of a feather.

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:37.940
<i>You're grouping us together?!</i>

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.310
But why five minutes?

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:43.570
Well, if you went to wake someone up
and they were like, give me another hour...

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:44.820
...wouldn't you be pissed?

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.190
Well, that's true...

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:50.360
...but five minutes comes up
in a lot of other situations.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.950
Like, just wait five minutes!

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:53.160
You have a point.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.620
Maybe 'cause it isn't too long or too short?

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.750
Though the five-minute wait
for a train feels really long.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:00.960
Sure does!

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:02.540
Guess so.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:03.790
But then again...

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:05.880
People who say to wait five minutes...

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.720
...tend to make you wait a lot longer.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:13.720
You know how people say to not use
your cell or put on makeup on the train?

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:18.640
But it's a lot worse when the
person next to you leans on you.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:20.520
They're so heavy.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.900
And you end up wanting to
stand after managing to get a seat.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:27.940
And when you're stuck with
the sticky head of an old person...

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:31.740
Sometimes, I try to shove them off...

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:36.330
...but they somehow manage to
keep returning to the same position.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:37.450
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:38.620
It's a mystery.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:40.750
When I fall asleep...

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:44.210
...and there's a man on one
side and an empty seat on the other...

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.840
...I try to lean myself towards the empty seat...

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:50.130
...but for some reason, I always
end up leaning the other way.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:54.100
Guess your body feels more
comfortable leaning a certain way.

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.390
When I see someone leaning over...

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.020
...I shrink up like this...

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:02.690
...then their elbow hits my side.

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:05.230
Doesn't that mean they're actually awake?

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:06.610
Really?

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:07.400
Well...

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.230
Bye-bee!

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:09.150
Goodbye.

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:11.150
You know how...

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:13.450
...some people at our school
take the inbound train home...

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:16.080
...and some people take the outbound train home?

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:22.080
Don't the ones who take the
inbound train look more refined somehow?

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.790
Since Yuki-chan's an inbounder.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:25.500
That's not...

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.540
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:29.380
Back to the farm, fellas.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:52.700
<i>Oh.</i>

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:54.530
<i>This is the stop before.</i>

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:01.000
Yo!

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.080
I didn't get any studying done yesterday.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:09.300
I actually put in a lot of effort this time.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:10.960
If I do say so myself.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:13.420
How much studying did you do?

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:15.220
A whole four hours!
Only four hours.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:16.970
Huh?

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:21.180
You're good at everything, Kagami.

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:24.270
Well, I do a lot of studying.

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:25.520
Just between you and me.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:29.110
You're definitely really competitive.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:30.070
Well...

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:32.400
Maybe it's my pride as the older sister...

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:36.780
I feel like I have to be ahead of Tsukasa.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:39.620
Though I usually say neither
of us is really older or younger.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:41.580
I used to be pretty worried about that stuff.

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:45.750
But Tsukasa probably wasn't much competition.

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:47.540
Well, that's true...

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:48.960
<i>Stupid Kona-chan thinks she's all that!</i>

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:51.500
It's almost Christmas!

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:54.220
I wonder what my present will be this year.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:56.260
You still get presents...

00:07:57.130 --> 00:08:00.470
How long did you believe in Santa Claus?

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:04.730
Santa Claus isn't real?

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:05.560
<i>Holy cow!</i>

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:08.940
Santa never came to Konata's house...

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:12.070
...so her dad gave her presents in his stead.

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:15.030
That's why she thought he might be out there.

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:16.030
That old man...

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:18.570
He really wants to look good
in front of his daughter, huh?

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:20.490
Hey, Hiiragi!

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:22.330
Hiiragi-san.

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:23.660
Here's the handout from before.

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:24.790
Gotcha.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.790
And then, Hiiragi-chan...

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:28.870
Hiiragi!

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:30.170
You dropped your pencil.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:31.290
Thanks.

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:33.210
Hey, Kagami!

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:34.800
Kagami-san.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.300
Here's the handout from earlier.

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:37.380
Got it.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.890
Sebastian, like, stinks.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:41.220
Kagami.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.470
You dropped your handkerchief.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:43.470
Holy cow?

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.850
<i>Maybe I go to Tsukasa's class a little too much.</i>

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:51.230
My cavity started hurting recently.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.690
My, how dreadful.

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:55.190
I really can't stand dentists.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:58.280
You went to see the dentist
for your cavity the other day.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:08:59.700
Is it better now?

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:04.290
Dentists take a long time on each tooth...

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:06.790
...and they have to repeat
the procedure for every tooth...

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:09.460
...so it takes a long time, right?

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:12.290
So I ended up escaping...

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:13.670
...after making a number of excuses.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:15.300
What to do?

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:16.760
<i>She sounded all cutesy...</i>

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.630
<i>...but that's pretty crazy!</i>

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:19.930
Konata!

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:23.010
Wanna go wild with everyone on Christmas?

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:23.970
Sorry.

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:25.850
I already have plans for Christmas.

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:26.970
Oh.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:28.140
Is it a man?

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:29.690
Something like that.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:32.900
Are you going somewhere with your dad?

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:33.480
Nope.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:36.230
I told Dad that I'd be home late.

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:37.490
Don't tell me...

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:39.610
You're really going on a date with your boyfriend?

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:40.490
When did you...

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:42.240
Sorry to disappoint you...

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.740
...but I'm just working.

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:44.990
Oh...

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:48.250
Almost all the customers are male so I wasn't lying.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.040
Thought you'd managed to get ahead of us.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.170
You got me.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:54.040
There's a special event on Christmas.

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:57.380
We dress like Santa CIaus for that.

00:09:57.670 --> 00:09:59.880
You really love that kind of stuff, huh?

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:01.380
But you know...

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:04.930
You guys also cosplay as
shrine maidens for New Year's.

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:06.390
At your temple.

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:07.850
Don't call it cosplay.

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:10.140
Anyway...

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:12.060
It's good that Santa Claus gives everyone presents...

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:17.150
...but ever since I was little,
I was like, he's totally trespassing.

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:20.190
You shouldn't look down on
something based on a holy man.

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:21.860
Spiteful brat.

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:22.610
Still...

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.830
Santa is supposed to give children dreams...

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:32.460
...so what's with the men who
turn to this squirt with their dreams?

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:33.420
What's this?

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.540
You just casually insulted a lot of people?

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:39.090
And is it okay for you guys to celebrate Christmas?

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:39.710
Oh, yeah.

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:42.420
We usually got Christmas presents, right?

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:45.430
We worship every god there is.

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:48.220
We regularly visit temples.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:51.230
And we sang in a church choir once.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:53.980
Sounds peaceful.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:54.770
But...

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:55.440
Yes?
But...

00:10:55.440 --> 00:11:00.690
A shrine maiden said she wanted
to get married in a wedding dress...

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:02.570
Is that okay?

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:04.950
Wouldn't that be a little complicated?

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:09.330
Yo!

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:11.000
Getting chilly these days.

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:13.040
Cousin Yui, welcome!

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:14.290
Whatcha watching?

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:16.420
A detective show.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:17.960
Any good?

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:18.880
Not really.

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:19.880
Nothing else to do.

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:21.920
Okay, I got it.

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:23.420
That man's the killer.

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.260
Please wait, Officer.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.550
There's something odd about this case.

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:28.970
Nothing odd at all.

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:30.390
Case closed!

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:31.100
What's with you?

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:31.970
This has nothing to do with you.

00:11:33.230 --> 00:11:35.850
This is why cops are useless.

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:37.980
<i>Aren't you a cop yourself...</i>

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:41.690
Why'd someone have to call now?

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:44.320
They're about to reveal the killer.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:45.570
How can you tell?

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:45.860
Look.

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:46.660
I see.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.490
You're the killer, huh?

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:49.870
No use in hiding it now.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:54.460
I wonder why these two-hour
shows always end on the edge of a cliff.

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:59.630
Maybe cause people aren't willing to
act until their back's against the wall?

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:01.130
Yahoo!

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:02.250
How ya doing?

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:03.800
Cousin Yui, evenin'.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:05.510
Whatcha watchin'?

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:07.470
A movie for a popular detective show.

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:09.140
Dad rented it.

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:11.810
Crimes don't happen in conference rooms!

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:13.020
They happen at the scene!

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:14.600
No, no, that's wrong.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.640
Nobody ever gets that passionate.

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:18.270
<i>Yet you reject that...</i>

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:19.560
Pretty sure that...

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:24.070
...the receipts were stolen at the behest of the chief.

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:26.780
This is why he fails.

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:28.570
<i>You know what's going on?</i>

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:29.570
That's right...

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:31.530
They eat pork bowls a lot in police shows...

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:33.410
...but apparently, that isn't actually allowed.

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:34.830
Well, it's fiction...

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:36.210
...so a lot of it's probably made-up.

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:40.460
So police commissioners'
granddaughters aren't really like that?!

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.540
Police commissioners' granddaughters?

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:44.380
Well, I've never met one.

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:46.510
I'd at least want Mai-chan to exist...

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:47.550
To give me hope...

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:49.340
Empty dream.

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:53.930
There sure are a lot of cases
with adults going after children.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:55.140
Indeed...

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.730
I've been thinking...

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:59.600
If you teach kids martial arts...

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:01.730
...wouldn't there be a decrease in that stuff?

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:04.530
After intensive training...

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:08.530
...Master Oyama was able to beat a
cow with his bare hands, with one blow.

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:11.450
And bears toppled like trees after a couple of hits!

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:12.620
I see.

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:16.370
But won't that come back to haunt you?

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:17.870
When those kids grow up...

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:19.420
...the adults will be strong, too.

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:21.670
U-Um...

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:23.000
You know...

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:24.630
People say training in the martial arts...

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.880
...helps you mature as a person.

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:28.880
I see.

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:29.630
But...

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:33.970
There's someone who does martial
arts and hasn't matured right here.

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:35.640
How rude!

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:36.850
Oh.

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:41.650
I have this cousin, Cousin Yui's little
sister, who's entering high school next year.

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:42.940
She's physically weak...

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:43.310
Cousin Konata!

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:46.360
...but she's sweet and pure and really adorable.

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:53.160
But when I start thinking about how a
healthy spirit leads to a healthy body...

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:58.290
....I start feeling like something dark
is lurking behind those shining eyes.

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:00.910
I doubt aphorisms are universal.

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:02.170
Look at you.

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:04.290
The year's almost over.

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:07.920
Once it's December, you always
feel like the year flew by so fast.

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:11.970
Are you going to help out at your
temple as shrine maidens again this year?

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:13.010
Probably.

00:14:13.010 --> 00:14:14.930
Come draw your fortune again.

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:16.260
With fortunes...

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:20.060
If you get really bad luck, it's an unpleasant feeling.

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:21.390
But if you get really good luck...

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:24.810
...it feels like you already wasted
your luck for the year, doesn't it?

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:27.980
Well, that's why people say average luck is best.

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:29.230
Okay!

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:31.610
Then here's an early present from your teacher!

00:14:31.610 --> 00:14:32.950
Here are your report cards!

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:35.530
Here! Good work!
How did you do, Kona-chan?

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:37.490
Teacher!

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:39.290
I don't want this present!

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:43.420
We give presents based on effort in my school of Santa.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:44.710
Think on it.

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:47.210
Like a bonus to your winter homework.

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:50.960
I wonder what kind of Christmas
cakes will be good this year!

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:52.380
When you go to a bakery...

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:54.260
...there are so many cute cakes...

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:57.100
...that you can have fun just looking.

00:14:57.100 --> 00:15:00.680
What happens to the cakes
that weren't sold before Christmas?

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:04.190
Perhaps the employees take them home.

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:08.230
But if nobody takes them,
they might throw them away.

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:11.860
They often compare marriage to Christmas.

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:13.820
Like how twenty-five is the end of the line.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:17.990
Once you're past twenty-five,
a Christmas cake is just another cake.

00:15:17.990 --> 00:15:20.990
After one night, it's just another decorated cake...

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:22.540
...that suddenly looks stale...

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:24.790
...so you lose your appetite.

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:28.590
I was talking about Santa Claus
with Kona-chan the other day.

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:30.880
How long did you believe in Santa, Yuki-chan?

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:34.880
It feels like you would have
been a true believer like me.

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:37.590
I also believed in Santa Claus.

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:41.680
When I was little, I tried to send a
letter of gratitude to Santa Claus...

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:44.100
...and did some research.

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:47.230
But I didn't learn much after asking my parents...

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:49.110
...so I did some thorough investigating...

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.440
...and learned of the people Santa Claus was based on...

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:54.150
...and once I saw the phrase
"origin of Santa Claus" pop up...

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:56.860
...my dreams were quickly shattered.

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:00.530
How'd you do, Miyuki-san?

00:16:00.530 --> 00:16:01.540
Lemme see!

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:04.040
Just what you would expect from Yuki-chan.

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:05.410
I could never do so well.

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:08.920
I feel a little pissed about losing...

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:12.550
Yuki-chan's at the top of our class so it's hopeless...

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:14.170
We could never beat her.

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:14.970
No.

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:16.880
I don't care about grades...

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:17.840
...but stuff like bust size...

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:18.800
Look! Whoa!

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:21.600
<i>I'm hungry.</i>

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:23.560
<i>I'll have a cup of ramen.</i>

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:24.930
<i>Not done yet?</i>

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:28.770
<i>These three minutes of waiting feel really long.</i>

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:31.570
<i>I'll use this to kill time today.</i>

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:35.030
And then your noodles end up soggy, right?

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:35.860
Me too!

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:38.490
The extra broth for my cup fried soba dried up!

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:39.570
You people...

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:45.620
<i>She told me she would be late...</i>

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:46.660
<i>But this is too late!</i>

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:48.580
<i>I can't let her make a habit of this.</i>

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:50.710
<i>Need to give her a stern
dressing down every now and then.</i>

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:52.290
<i>As the man of the house.</i>

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:53.880
I'm home!

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:54.590
Konata!

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:55.510
Come here for a minute!

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:56.880
What time do you think it i—

00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:58.130
Merry Christmas!

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:01.720
This is my Christmas present for you.

00:17:02.050 --> 00:17:04.140
It must have been cold outside!

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:05.350
Want some hot tea?

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:05.850
Yay!

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:06.890
I do! I do!

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:09.440
I'm so happy I could die.

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:10.520
Yo!

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:11.980
G'day!

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:14.980
Cousin Yui's here to save the day!

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:16.320
You stink of alcohol!

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:17.820
It's dangerous to DUI!

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:21.320
I parked the car somewhere and had a drink nearby.

00:17:21.320 --> 00:17:22.490
Listen to me!

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:25.370
It's Christmas Eve yet my husband's not here!

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:27.200
Our plans tonight are...

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:27.790
Cousin Yui...

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:30.210
Shouldn't you go to your parents'
place instead every once in a while?

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:33.090
Hello?

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:33.750
Yui?

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:34.840
It's me.

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:36.710
I was going to sneak in and surprise you...

00:17:36.710 --> 00:17:38.030
...but it was locked.

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:39.510
Are you at your parents' place?

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:40.380
I'm coming home!

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:42.470
Right away at full speed!

00:17:42.470 --> 00:17:44.350
Running every light on the way!

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:47.390
Seriously, you shouldn't be breaking the law.

00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:48.640
I'll drive you.

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:51.020
I've got a little time.

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:52.850
I'll log in for a sec.

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:53.520
Huh?

00:17:53.520 --> 00:17:54.850
Teacher's on.

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:00.150
Teacher.

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:01.410
Let's go crazy.

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:03.570
Until morning.

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:07.700
Please wait one moment.

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:16.920
<i>Ain't a leftover.</i>

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:18.670
<i>Doesn't count as a leftover.</i>

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:20.090
<i>'Cause I bought one.</i>

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:25.010
I was here last Sunday to buy manga.

00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:27.890
Don't get why you pay the fare to come here so much.

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:29.220
Even if it's for the points...

00:18:29.220 --> 00:18:30.390
...this is pretty excessive.

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:31.520
You really love this stuff.

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:35.690
Besides, do you even use the prizes they give?

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:37.520
I don't.

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:38.900
Thought so.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:41.280
That kind of stuff is hard to use.

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:42.450
Yep. Yep.

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:44.530
lt'd be a waste to use.

00:18:44.530 --> 00:18:46.490
Their value would go down.

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:48.990
<i>Oh, so that's how it is...</i>

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:49.750
<i>Whatever.</i>

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:54.790
No!

00:18:54.790 --> 00:18:55.540
Yes.

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:58.170
Didn't you get shocked by static electricity?

00:18:58.170 --> 00:18:59.000
Nope.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:00.630
Why's that?

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:03.300
Konata's always sitting in front of the computer...

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:05.760
...so her body's already full of weird waves?

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:08.060
Still, I really can't stand winter.

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:11.390
And I heard you can get shocked
just by touching someone's hand.

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:12.230
Ow!

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:15.020
Are you sure you two don't really hate each other?

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:15.060
Holy cow.

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:15.940
Ow!
Holy cow.

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:22.110
Whatcha doing?

00:19:22.110 --> 00:19:23.990
Oh, I wanted to try it again!

00:19:25.030 --> 00:19:27.030
Stronger!

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:34.040
Good lucky!

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:37.460
I'm your navigator, Akira Kogami!

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:40.460
We're already on the eleventh
episode of Lucky Channel!

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:42.130
And on this eleventh episode...

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:47.430
...I have some wonderful news
you've all been waiting for!

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:48.260
U-Uh...

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:49.600
Everybody's sent in...

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:50.430
She's really in it today.

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:53.390
...lots of passionate letters...

00:19:53.390 --> 00:19:56.770
...asking for Akira to show up in the actual show!

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:57.190
H-Hello.

00:19:57.190 --> 00:19:57.730
On the next episode, I, Akira Kogami...

00:19:57.730 --> 00:19:59.400
I'm the assistant Minoru Shiraishi.

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:00.360
Zip it!

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:01.110
...will be showing up in the actual show!

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:03.110
But I need to introduce myself!

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:07.570
Thank you to Konata Izumi from
Saitama along with everyone else...

00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:09.240
...who sent postcards to Newtype!

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.330
So Akira-sama's also making an appearance?

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:15.830
What's with the...

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:18.250
"Like, you're finally showing up
in the twelfth episode?

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.380
I've been in it for, like, forever!

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:21.460
Ho. Ho. Ho."

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:22.630
...attitude you've got?

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:24.210
A-Absolutely not!

00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:27.800
It's an honor to appear with
Akira-sama in the actual show as well!

00:20:28.970 --> 00:20:29.930
Appear?

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:32.640
All you did this week was
pick up a handkerchief, yeah?

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:37.350
You shouldn't be thinking you've got
what it takes to make it in this business!

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:40.150
Don't forget that you can just disappear like that!

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:42.520
I-I'll keep that in mind.

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:44.780
After that announcement...

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:46.190
...you can't wait for the next episode!

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:48.610
You want it now?

00:20:48.610 --> 00:20:49.450
Everyone is probably trembling...

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:51.370
Er, shaking naked in their boots in anticipation!

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:52.030
Hey.

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:54.040
We should treat our fans with care...

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:57.040
...and air it right now!

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:57.410
We can grab a thirty minute slot, right?

00:20:57.410 --> 00:20:58.580
Uh...

00:20:58.580 --> 00:20:59.540
That'd be pushing it...
We can grab a thirty minute slot, right?

00:20:59.540 --> 00:21:01.290
Pretty please?
That'd be pushing it...

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:03.300
Or forget it.

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:07.550
So send any messages to the
radio show or the home page!

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:09.470
Bye-bee!

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:12.010
What to do?

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:14.140
It'd be bad if I overshadowed
the main characters, right?

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:15.430
It would indeed.

00:21:15.430 --> 00:21:17.600
But there's a tendency for the
main character's friends and rivals...

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:21.810
...to end up more popular than
the actual main characters!

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:23.520
What?

00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:24.400
A-Akira-sama?

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:25.360
What's wrong?

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:25.980
Aren't you...

00:21:25.980 --> 00:21:26.490
Yes?

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:27.240
...talking about yourself?

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:30.740
Don't get so full of yourself
'cause you're popular lately!

00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:31.530
No, absolutely not!

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:33.160
Don't expect this to last!

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:33.740
No, never!

00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:35.200
You won't be placing first in the poll

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:36.160
What are you talking about?!

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:36.830
Don't mess with me!

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:38.080
That's impossible.

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:38.790
Listen to m—
Don't mess with me!

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:49.930
Next we have a duet from Tsukasa and Miyuki-san.

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:50.760
Yuki-chan.

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:52.380
Let's go up front to sing.

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:56.930
You chose a song for them to sing...

00:21:56.930 --> 00:21:58.020
How bizarre.

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:00.640
I know all kinds of songs.

00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:05.110
But it's still an anime song, huh?

00:22:05.110 --> 00:22:08.570
Anime songs actually come
in handy in these situations.

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:43.650
Not even close!

00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:13.340
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:13.900 --> 00:23:14.340
I'm Tsukasa.

00:23:15.090 --> 00:23:15.840
Um...

00:23:15.840 --> 00:23:19.470
I was really hungry one night...

00:23:19.470 --> 00:23:21.220
...but it was really late...

00:23:21.220 --> 00:23:24.270
...so I was wondering if I should eat something...

00:23:24.270 --> 00:23:27.810
I finally decided a little bite would be okay.

00:23:27.810 --> 00:23:29.570
And then I went to the kitchen...

00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:31.860
...and I remembered I had some snacks left over...

00:23:31.860 --> 00:23:33.490
...so I opened up the freezer...

00:23:33.490 --> 00:23:34.570
I'm already out of time?!

00:23:35.030 --> 00:23:35.740
Next time:

00:23:35.740 --> 00:23:37.070
Let's Go to the Festival.

00:23:37.070 --> 00:23:38.530
Look forward to next time!
